  "tiles": [
    {
      "tile_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context",
      "title": "Prioritizing Findings and Framing Recommendations",
      "summary": "Learn to lead a stakeholder report with the finding most relevant to the decision, frame a recommendation that is distinct from the finding itself, and open the narrative with a short context section that level-sets the reader.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s01",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Prioritizing Findings",
          "title": "Lead with what the decision-maker needs, not what surprised you most",
          "lede": "A delivery-times analysis can surface many findings. Choosing which one opens the report is a judgment call — and the right criterion is the stakeholder's decision, not analytical novelty.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s01.b1",
              "role": "intro",
              "text": "A full look at QuickShip delivery times might surface several findings: Lagos slowed down, Kano's times are the most variable, one courier is unusually fast. Not all of them belong at the top of the report to the Head of Operations.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#tb1"
                ],
                "fact_ids": []
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s01.b2",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "The engagement and scoping stage should establish how the analysis will inform decisions. That decision — whether to add Lagos couriers — points to which finding matters most: the Lagos slowdown, not the courier with the fastest times. Crafting a communication's big idea requires knowing what is not essential and boiling the overall message down to a single sentence that captures its core.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#tb2",
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#tb3"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#f1",
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#f2"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s01.b3",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "Writing about data should only include information relevant to the audience. The operations manager's decision about Lagos staffing does not require the full breakdown of every city's variability. Relevance to the decision — not analytical novelty — is the right criterion.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#tb3"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#f2",
                  "stakeholder.prioritizing_findings_by_relevance#f3"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "side_by_side",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s01.b4",
              "left_label": "Ordered by analytical interestingness",
              "right_label": "Ordered by relevance to the staffing decision",
              "left": {
                "type": "data_table",
                "asset_ref": {
                  "asset_id": "ds_city_delivery_summary",
                  "variant_id": null,
                  "columns": [
                    "city",
                    "avg_delivery_min",
                    "variability_rank",
                    "finding_priority"
                  ]
                },
                "caption": "Findings ranked by what is most analytically notable",
                "highlight": [
                  {
                    "target": {
                      "kind": "row",
                      "row": {
                        "where": {
                          "city": "Kano"
                        }
                      }
                    },
