        {
          "step_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s06",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Framing Recommendations",
          "title": "A finding tells you what happened; a recommendation says what to do",
          "lede": "Restating a finding more emphatically is not a recommendation. A recommendation names the action and what the reader is being asked to approve.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s06.b1",
              "role": "intro",
              "text": "\"Lagos delivery times rose to 30 minutes\" is a finding — it describes what the data shows. \"We recommend adding one more courier to the Lagos route\" is a recommendation: it states what should happen next. The two are easy to confuse, but a stakeholder needs both.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#tb1"
                ],
                "fact_ids": []
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s06.b2",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "The value of analytical efforts is only truly realized when the insights discovered are acted upon. An audience cannot be assumed to find the intended takeaway as obvious as the presenter thinks it is. Simply restating the Lagos finding more emphatically may not tell the manager what to do — the recommendation needs to say so explicitly.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#tb2"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#f1"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s06.b3",
              "role": "example",
              "text": "A well-formed recommendation makes clear to the audience what they need to know and what they are being asked to do. \"We recommend adding one Lagos courier; please approve the added headcount\" states the action and names the explicit ask, so the Head of Operations knows exactly what decision is in front of them.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#tb3"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#f2"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "before_after",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.s06.b4",
              "before": {
                "type": "diagram",
                "diagram_kind": "container",
                "title": "Finding only (weak)",
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "id": "finding_only",
                    "label": "Lagos delivery times rose to 30 minutes — above the 25-minute target.",
                    "kind": "finding"
                  }
                ],
                "alt_text": "A text box showing only the finding: 'Lagos delivery times rose to 30 minutes — above the 25-minute target.' No action is stated."
              },
              "after": {
                "type": "diagram",
                "diagram_kind": "container",
                "title": "Finding + recommendation (strong)",
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "id": "finding_node",
                    "label": "Finding: Lagos delivery times rose to 30 minutes — above the 25-minute target.",
                    "kind": "finding"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "recommendation_node",
                    "label": "Recommendation: We recommend adding one Lagos courier; please approve the added headcount.",
                    "kind": "recommendation"
                  }
                ],
                "alt_text": "Two text boxes: the finding ('Lagos delivery times rose to 30 minutes — above the 25-minute target') followed by a distinct recommendation ('We recommend adding one Lagos courier; please approve the added headcount'), showing the structural difference between restating data and stating an action."
              },
              "change_summary": "Adding an explicit recommendation — naming the action and the ask — transforms a finding into something the Head of Operations can act on.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#tb1",
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#tb2",
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#tb3"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#f1",
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#f2"
                ],
                "anchors": [
                  "stakeholder.actionable_recommendation_framing#visual"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
