          "eyebrow": "Let's revisit",
          "title": "Short opener vs. lengthy background — the contrast",
          "lede": "The opening context section should be short and purposeful, not a page of background before the findings.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stakeholder_prioritizing_framing_context.r03.b1",
              "role": "example",
              "text": "A weak opener spends a paragraph on company history, technical definitions, and methodology before the reader knows what the report is about. A strong opener uses two sentences: one states what the report covers and why the analysis was done; the second names the specific question it answers. For the QuickShip delivery report: \"This report examines delivery times across Lagos, Kano, and Abuja last quarter, prompted by rising customer complaints about Lagos deliveries. It answers: which zones are missing the 25-minute target, and by how much?\"",
